/**
\mainpage Qore PDF Module

\section intro Introduction

The `pdf` module provides PDF functionality for Qore using QPDF and PoDoFo,
with optional PDFium support for rendering and text extraction.

\section features Features

- Create PDFs with PoDoFo
- Read/edit/merge/split PDFs with QPDF
- Optional rendering and text extraction with PDFium
- Data provider actions for Qorus integration

\section dataprov Data Provider Actions

The module ships with PdfDataProvider for Qore's data provider framework.
Example `qdp` commands:

\code{.bash}
qdp 'pdf{}/document/create' output_path=out.pdf,page_count=2
qdp 'pdf{}/document/info' input_path=out.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/metadata' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=meta.pdf,metadata='{"title":"Updated"}'
qdp 'pdf{}/document/merge' inputs='("a.pdf","b.pdf")',output_path=merged.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/rotate' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=rotated.pdf,pages='(0)',degrees=90
qdp 'pdf{}/render/page' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0,dpi=150
qdp 'pdf{}/render/extract-text' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0
\endcode

\section dependencies Dependencies

- QPDF (required)
- PoDoFo (required; bundled by default, LGPL-2.0-or-later)
- PDFium (optional)

\section releasenotes Release Notes

- 2026-01-20: Bundled PoDoFo to include a fix for a CFF font-embedding leak in
  the AFDKO subsetting path; optional PDFium remains unchanged.

\section license License

MIT License
*/
